==========================================================
1. PRODUCT VISION
==========================================================

FutureSchool is a digital operating platform for schools.

The objective is to replace fragmented/manual school processes such as:

- Student admissions
- Attendance registers
- Homework tracking
- Exam schedules
- Marks entry
- Report Card preparation
- Fee collection
- Payment receipts
- Hall Tickets
- Parent communication
- Teacher communication
- Leave requests
- Parent-Teacher meetings
- Transport
- Student pickup authorization
- School notices
- Complaints
- Consent forms
- School events
- Staff operations
- Academic planning
- Administrative approvals
- Audit records

with one secure role-based platform.

FutureSchool must feel like a serious modern SaaS application, not a colorful children's educational app.

==========================================================
2. USERS
==========================================================

FutureSchool has five main portal experiences:

1. STUDENT
2. PARENT
3. TEACHER
4. PRINCIPAL
5. ADMIN

These portals have different permissions and responsibilities.

Never treat them as the same dashboard with renamed menus.

==========================================================
3. MULTI-SCHOOL ARCHITECTURE
==========================================================

FutureSchool is intended to support multiple schools.

Conceptually:

FutureSchool
    |
    +-- School A
    |
    +-- School B
    |
    +-- School C

Every school has its own:

- Students
- Parents
- Teachers
- Principal
- Admin users
- Academic years
- Classes
- Sections
- Subjects
- Timetables
- Exams
- Fees
- Payments
- Transport
- Policies
- Branding
- Integrations

For the frontend prototype, use mock school context.

Architect the frontend so tenant/school context can later come from a real backend.

Never build UI architecture that assumes there will only ever be one school.

